      "heading": "B — Audience",
      "learner_facing": false,
      "markdown": "## B — Audience, Section Nine Speed and right of way\n\nThe audience is first-time, never-licensed applicants preparing for the West Virginia Class E knowledge examination, reading at a plain-English level with no prior driving knowledge assumed. Section Nine teaches how fast the law allows and how to communicate speed and direction changes to other drivers. It depends on the traffic signs chapter for speed limit and advisory signs and on the definitions chapter for the school zone and highway terms. The rules progress from the basic speed law and designated limits, through driving slowly, to turn signals, hand signals and hand position.\n",
